==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|dowbly}}, {{m|enm|doubli}}, {{m|enm|dubli}}, {{m|enm|doubeliche}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|double|ly}}.<ref>{{cite-web
|url=http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/doubly
|title=doubly
|lang=en
|publisher=Random House, Inc.
|accessdate=2014-12-02
}}</ref>

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|usually|of relative importance|of degree, quantity or measure}} In a [[double]] manner; twice the severity or degree.
#* {{RQ:Adams Hitchhiker|2}}
#*: Time is an illusion. Lunchtime '''doubly''' so.
#: {{ux|en|My mother was always '''doubly''' careful when winding the grandfather clock.}}
# In [[two]] [[ways]]
#: {{ux|en|Stealing and then lying about it is '''doubly''' wrong.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} with [[duplicity]]

